      "id": "n-hud",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -132,
      "w": 560,
      "page": "capture",
      "text": "Landmarks are the only thing that places a capture on the plan (ADR-0026), so the tap is the interaction to get right.\nOne tap means three things: hitting a mark selects it, a tap while selected moves it, anything else places a new one."
    },
    {
      "id": "n-nochrome",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": -132,
      "w": 430,
      "page": "capture",
      "text": "No fake status bar or keyboard anywhere \u2014 the real ones render on top on device. The 59 pt at the top is left empty on purpose."
    },
    {
      "id": "n-motif",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -132,
      "w": 520,
      "page": "screens",
      "text": "Motif: the section cut. A room is a wall face; capturing it cuts it open, and the opening is the coverage.\nPhase is never carried by colour \u2014 green/amber/red stay semantic."
    },
    {
      "id": "n-plan",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 560,
      "page": "plan",
      "text": "The two screens that did not exist before. Plan import is drawn as a phone photo of a drawing taped to a stud wall, because that is the real case.\nPlan coverage answers \u201cwhat have I missed\u201d spatially \u2014 a count cannot tell you the far corner of the great room was never walked."
    }
